From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odonnellmatt <odonnellmatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:01:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/pad: place and size the touch controls by groups
 (DM_TOUCH_GROUPS)

The touch controls could be moved one by one in the shell's touch layout
editor (DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT, in quarter-key steps) and given one size for all
of them (DM_TOUCH_SIZE), but nothing moved or resized a group of controls
as a whole. On an iPad held sideways the top row (ZL, L, L3 and ZR, R, R3)
sits far above the picture, and players ask to lower it and to make some
groups larger.

DmPadGeometry.h ("Groups") now places six groups as a whole: the left
shoulders (ZL, L, L3), the right ones (ZR, R, R3), the left stick, the
D-pad, A B X Y, and the middle (-, the menu button and +). DM_TOUCH_GROUPS
holds, per layout (2D, 3D, and both again below a portrait picture), a
place for each group and all controls' size, for example

  1;3d/all:110/lshoulder:0,430,120/rshoulder:1000,430,120

A place is an anchor in thousandths of the free range of the group's area
(the safe area; for the left stick, the D-pad and A B X Y the bottom
corners' area, which reaches halfway into the side insets, as before) and
a size in percent (50 to 200). All controls' size (50 to 150) scales the
base unit on top of DM_TOUCH_SIZE. So a stored place keeps the group on
the screen on every device and in every orientation, and a layout made on
an iPad keeps its proportions on an iPhone.

On a phone held sideways the sensor housing sits in the middle of a side
inset. The left stick, the D-pad and A B X Y reach halfway into the side
insets only in their built-in band: moved up or grown past it, a group
moves inward until each of its shapes above the band is inside the safe
area's sides (dm_pad_group_keep_off_sides; an iPad has no side insets, so
nothing moves there). On a 932 x 430 phone with 59-point insets the stick
lifted to the island's height has its ring from x 59, not 29.5.

A group is kept only where its shapes stay inside their area and clear of
every other group, by the gap and by the reach of a touch target past its
drawn shape, so a touch on a drawn control still goes to that control. A
group that does not fit tries sizes toward its built-in one, and one that
never fits stays where it is built in. No size takes a touch target under
44 points across unless the built-in one already is, all controls' size
included (dm_pad_all_floor). The stick's ring, knob and travel, every hit
radius, and L3 and R3 (one radius per side now) follow their group's size.
The value's syntax follows DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT's: an unknown layout, group or
field is skipped (a newer editor), anything else malformed, out of range
or longer than 1024 bytes is ignored whole.

DmPadEditing.h holds the rules of the in-game editor that comes next, pure
so that the tests drive them and every gesture goes through the same code:
a drag's place (snapped to the area's edges and middle), both sides
together (the two shoulder groups, and the left stick with A B X Y, move
together and size together as far as each has room, unless the player
picks each side on its own), the largest size
that fits, where Done saves (every game's layout or a game's own, keeping
the layouts the editor neither showed nor changed), which finger drags and
when two fingers pinch, and the editor's words in DM_PAD_EDIT_TEXT's order.

Nothing reads DM_TOUCH_GROUPS yet: DmGamepad.m only draws L3 and R3 with
their own radii. With no groups, empty groups or groups for another layout
the geometry is the one the gamepad drew before, bit for bit.

Checked: test_pad_geometry.py runs on Linux too now (clang, plain C against
pad_geometry/portable/UIKit/UIKit.h, which stands in for the few Core
Graphics rules the headers use), and runs the new pad_groups_check.m: the
value read, skipped, ignored and written back (20,000 random strings, 2,000
random drafts); the built-in layout bit for bit with no, empty or
other-layout groups; anchors 0 and 1000 at the area's edges; sizes, floors
and all controls on 810 layouts; 8,100 seeded random layouts that keep
every rule (inside, on screen, no overlap, placed groups clear, every touch
point taken by the control it lies in); the editor's drag, mirror, refusal,
sizes, scopes and fingers; an 11-inch iPad with its top row lowered; on
every phone held sideways the stick, the D-pad and A B X Y lifted or grown
keep their shapes above the band out of the side insets, and an iPad's
value keeps its anchors there (15,349 geometries in all; also under gcc
ASan and UBSan, no reports). A dump of every geometry field and of the
hit-test, menu and locked-key decisions on a 3-point grid is byte-identical
before and after this change (3,528 cases: 21 screens, 2D and 3D, four
sizes, three stick places, seven DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT values). Not run here: the
same test against Apple's frameworks on a Mac.

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0020 and 0040: the seedds/nxnative pull request follows once they are upstream]
Reason: the in-game layout editor (the next patch) places and sizes touch controls by groups: DM_TOUCH_GROUPS, its rules and their tests; nothing changes without a stored value
